# M6.2 acceptance, run 1 of 2: File > Open Project (Ctrl+Shift+O), the
# project tree, opening a PDF from it, refresh after changes made outside the
# app, an unsaved project and "Save as project", File > Recent Projects.
# Run both runs with tests/acceptance/m6.2.sh, which builds the fixture in
# /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2, a scratch HOME and a logging fake sidecar
# (tests/acceptance/m6.2-fake-sidecar.sh), and checks the sidecar log and the
# .reader/ folders after each run. This run is
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <out>/run1 -s tests/acceptance/m6.2.steps -- \
#     env HOME=/tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/home \
#       READER_SIDECAR_CMD=<worktree>/tests/acceptance/m6.2-fake-sidecar.sh \
#       READER_FAKE_LOG=/tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/fake-run1.log \
#       ./build/app/agentic-reader
#
# Fixture (F = /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2), no .reader/ anywhere at the start:
#   F/proj/alpha.pdf, beta.PDF      tests/data/sample.pdf (3 pages, "Page One")
#   F/proj/notes.txt, readme.md     not PDFs
#   F/proj/papers/long.pdf          tests/data/long.pdf (520 pages,
#                                   "Page 1 of 520" heading)
#   F/proj/papers/data.csv          not a PDF
#   F/proj/papers/deep/nested.pdf   tests/data/color.pdf (1 small page)
#   F/proj/empty/                   no files
#   F/proj/misc/todo.txt            no PDF
#   F/proj/.hidden/secret.pdf       hidden folder
#   F/loose/single.pdf              sample.pdf, outside any project
#   F/loose/other.txt               not a PDF
#   F/src/sample.pdf, F/src/notes.txt   sources for the copies below
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (the implementer conforms or
# files a TEST DISPUTE):
#   - File menu, top to bottom: "&Open...\tCtrl+O", "Open &Project...\t
#     Ctrl+Shift+O", the "&Recent" files submenu (M2.5), a "Recent Pro&jects"
#     submenu, then "&Quit\tCtrl+Q". In an open File menu, J opens Recent
#     Projects. Its items are numbered like Recent files: "&1 <name or path>",
#     most recent first, so digit keys pick them.
#   - Open Project shows a wxDirDialog (a GTK folder chooser). The steps press
#     Alt+Home (GTK's "go to Home folder") first, because a chooser that starts
#     in "Recent" ignores a typed location, then type the folder's absolute
#     path into the location bar (Ctrl+L) with no trailing slash and press
#     Return, which selects that folder. The space/Home/End trick is the one
#     from tests/acceptance/m2.5.steps.
#   - Opening a folder with Open Project makes it a saved project at once: its
#     .reader/ exists right after the dialog closes. It goes to the top of
#     Recent Projects.
#   - A project (saved or unsaved) that becomes the open project sends
#     `open_project {path}` once, with the folder's absolute path and no
#     trailing slash. Opening a PDF that belongs to the open project sends
#     none.
#   - The project panel replaces the left "Project" placeholder (x 0..220,
#     y 69..875 at 1400x900). It has a header at the top and below it a
#     wxTreeCtrl that fills the rest of the pane, so (110, 700) is a blank
#     point inside the tree. The tree's root is hidden (wxTR_HIDE_ROOT): its
#     top-level rows are the project folder's entries. Every folder is shown
#     expanded, after opening and after every refresh.
#   - Tree content and order follow tests/test_project_panel.cpp: folders and
#     PDFs only, folders without a PDF below are left out, hidden folders and
#     .reader/ are skipped, subfolders before PDFs, each sorted by name.
#   - Clicking the blank point focuses the tree. Home selects the first row,
#     Down moves one row, Return activates the selected row
#     (wxEVT_TREE_ITEM_ACTIVATED, the same as a double click). Activating a
#     PDF opens it in the PDF pane like File > Open; activating a folder does
#     not open anything.
#   - Header: for a saved project it shows the project folder's name (here
#     "proj" or "loose"), with no "Unsaved project" text and no button. For an
#     unsaved project it says "Unsaved project" and has a wxButton labelled
#     "&Save as project", so Alt+S presses it wherever the focus is in the
#     main window. After saving, the header turns into the saved form.
#   - A PDF opened outside any project (File > Open here) opens its folder as
#     an unsaved project: the tree shows that folder, no .reader/ is created,
#     and it is not added to Recent Projects. "Save as project" creates
#     .reader/ and adds the folder to the top of Recent Projects.
#   - Opening a project, from Recent Projects or at start, also opens its
#     `open_file` when that file exists. When a project opens because a PDF
#     was opened (File > Open, drop, Recent), that PDF is shown instead.
#     Leaving a project (opening another
#     one, or quitting) saves its `open_file` in .reader/project.json.
#   - The refresh after a change outside the app shows within about 1 s
#     (300 ms debounce). The steps wait 1 s plus shot.sh's 0.3 s per step.
#     A folder created after the project opened is watched too.
#
# Geometry at 1400x900 (see m2.4.steps and m2.5.steps): menu bar y 0..27,
# toolbar y 28..68, left pane x 0..220, PDF pane x 225..980 and y 69..875,
# status bar y 876..900. Status field 0 (bottom left) is the open file's name.
wait 3

# Fresh start, no project yet (empty HOME): the left pane holds no tree rows
# (an empty pane or a short hint), the PDF pane holds no document, status
# field 0 does not name a file.
shot start

key ctrl+shift+o
wait 2

# Ctrl+Shift+O opened a GTK folder chooser over the window (a dialog to pick
# a folder, with a sidebar of places and a Cancel button). It is not the
# PDF file chooser: there is no "*.pdf" filter control.
shot project-dialog

key alt+Home
wait 1
key ctrl+l
wait 1
key space
key Home
run xdotool type --delay 0 /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj
key End BackSpace
wait 1
key Return
wait 3
run test -d /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/.reader

# The dialog is closed and proj is the open, saved project. The header names
# "proj" (no "Unsaved project", no button). The tree shows, top to bottom:
# papers, deep (indented under papers), nested.pdf (under deep), long.pdf
# (under papers), alpha.pdf, beta.PDF. Nothing else: no notes.txt,
# readme.md, data.csv, empty, misc, .hidden, secret.pdf or .reader. The PDF
# pane holds no document (proj has no open_file yet).
shot project-open

click 110 700
key Home Down Down Return
wait 3

# Activating the third row opened papers/deep/nested.pdf: the PDF pane shows
# color.pdf's single small coloured page, the toolbar entry reads "1 / 1",
# status field 0 "nested.pdf". The tree is unchanged, nested.pdf may be
# selected.
shot tree-open-nested

run cp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/src/sample.pdf /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/added.pdf
run cp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/src/notes.txt /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/added.txt
wait 1

# A PDF added from outside appears: papers, deep, nested.pdf, long.pdf,
# added.pdf, alpha.pdf, beta.PDF. added.txt does not appear. nested.pdf is
# still open, status field 0 "nested.pdf".
shot fs-added

run mv /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/alpha.pdf /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/omega.pdf
wait 1

# The rename shows: papers, deep, nested.pdf, long.pdf, added.pdf, beta.PDF,
# omega.pdf. No alpha.pdf.
shot fs-renamed

run rm /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/beta.PDF
wait 1

# The removal shows: papers, deep, nested.pdf, long.pdf, added.pdf,
# omega.pdf. No beta.PDF.
shot fs-removed

run mkdir /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/fresh
wait 1
run cp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/src/sample.pdf /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/proj/fresh/inside.pdf
wait 1

# A PDF added to a folder created after the project opened shows: fresh,
# inside.pdf (under fresh), papers, deep, nested.pdf, long.pdf, added.pdf,
# omega.pdf. nested.pdf is still open, status field 0 "nested.pdf".
shot fs-new-folder

key ctrl+o
wait 2
key alt+Home
wait 1
key ctrl+l
wait 1
key space
key Home
run xdotool type --delay 0 /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/loose/single.pdf
key End BackSpace
wait 1
key Return
wait 3
run test ! -e /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/loose/.reader

# A single PDF outside any project: single.pdf is open ("Page One", entry
# "1 / 3", status field 0 "single.pdf"). The header says "Unsaved project"
# and shows a "Save as project" button. The tree shows only single.pdf (no
# other.txt). No .reader/ was created in loose/ (checked by the run step).
shot unsaved-project

wait 2
run test ! -e /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/loose/.reader
key alt+s
wait 2
run test -d /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.2/loose/.reader

# "Save as project" created loose/.reader/ (checked by the run step). The
# header now names "loose", without "Unsaved project" and without the button.
# The tree still shows single.pdf, single.pdf is still open, status field 0
# "single.pdf".
shot saved-as-project

key alt+f
wait 1

# The File menu is open: "Open..." with Ctrl+O, "Open Project..." with
# Shift+Ctrl+O (GTK may write it as "Shift+Ctrl+O"), "Recent" with an arrow,
# "Recent Projects" with an arrow, and "Quit" with Ctrl+Q.
shot file-menu

key j
wait 1

# File > Recent Projects lists, numbered, most recent first: 1 loose, 2 proj
# (folder names or full paths). Nothing else: no papers, deep or fresh.
shot recent-projects

key 2
wait 3

# Recent Projects item 2 reopened proj and its open_file: the header names
# "proj", the tree is as in fs-new-folder (fresh, inside.pdf, papers, deep,
# nested.pdf, long.pdf, added.pdf, omega.pdf), nested.pdf is open (entry
# "1 / 1", status field 0 "nested.pdf").
shot recent-reopened

click 110 700
key Home Down Down Down Down Down Return
wait 3

# The sixth row, papers/long.pdf, is open: "Page 1 of 520" at the top of the
# PDF pane, entry "1 / 520", status field 0 "long.pdf". tests/acceptance/
# m6.2.sh checks that this shot exists.
shot tree-open-long

key ctrl+q
wait 3
